<Header BuildVersionNo="9.0.2.020.0" CharacterSet="AMERICAN_AMERICA.WE8ISO8859P1" CreationDate="21-NOV-01" DatabaseVersionNo="5.0.0.0.0.0" EulVersionNo="9.0.2.020.0" LastSavedDate="16-JAN-02" MinimumWebVersionNo="4.1" MinimumWindowsVersionNo="4.1" ProductVersionNo="9.0" WorkbookDescription="Hyper drill from Discoverer to find a Folder or Items Lineage in Oracle Warehouse Builder (OWB)" WorkbookDeveloperKey="LINEAGE" WorkbookName="Lineage" WorkbookOwner="" WorkbookVersionNo="1.0">
</Header>
<Sheet Background="" DeveloperKey="5" HasParamBitmap="True" Name="Lineage" ParamBitmap="" Showpageaxis="True" Title="&amp;Date&#x000d;&#x000a;OWB/Discoverer Lineage &#x000d;&#x000a;If Oracle Warehouse Builder (OWB) and Discoverer Bridge have been used to generate your Discoverer EUL, the Folder and Item Lineage will have been retained in the Discoverer EUL. &#x000d;&#x000a;Using this information you can now Hyper drill from this Discoverer Worksheet to the respective Folder or Item&apos;s Lineage held in OWB.&#x000d;&#x000a;First select the &apos;Business Area Name&apos; in the Page Item, then under the column &apos;Folder Lineage&apos;  or &apos;Item Lineage&apos; double click on the respective browser icon, this will then reveal the folder/ items lineage in OWB.&#x000d;&#x000a;To view the database tables and columns an item is derived from, Drill from the item &apos;Item Name&apos; to &apos;Database Column&apos;.&#x000d;&#x000a;&#x000d;&#x000a;Note: &#x000d;&#x000a;To enable the Hyper drill,  you will first need to run the Lineage.sql script. &#x000d;&#x000a;Please see the release notes or the install and configuration notes for further details." TitleAlign="Tiled" TitleBackColor="32896" TitleBitmapReference="" TitleDeveloperKey="60" TitleHtml="&lt;table width=&quot;100%&quot; border=0 cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=right&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;&amp;Date&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=center&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;&lt;u&gt;OWB/Discoverer Lineage &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;If Oracle Warehouse Builder (OWB) and Discoverer Bridge have been used to generate your Discoverer EUL, the Folder and Item Lineage will have been retained in the Discoverer EUL. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;Using this information you can now Hyper drill from this Discoverer Worksheet to the respective Folder or Item&apos;s Lineage held in OWB.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;First select the &apos;Business Area Name&apos; in the Page Item, then under the column &apos;Folder Lineage&apos;  or &apos;Item Lineage&apos; double click on the respective browser icon, this will then reveal the folder/ items lineage in OWB.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;To view the database tables and columns an item is derived from, Drill from the item &apos;Item Name&apos; to &apos;Database Column&apos;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;&lt;b&gt;Note: &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;&lt;b&gt;To enable the Hyper drill,  you will first need to run the Lineage.sql script. &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=1 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;&lt;b&gt;Please see the release notes or the install and configuration notes for further details.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;/table&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;" TitleRtf="{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang2057{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fcharset0 Arial;}}&#x000d;&#x000a;{\colortbl ;\red254\green255\blue255;}&#x000d;&#x000a;\viewkind4\uc1\pard\qr\cf1\f0\fs16 &amp;Date\ul &#x000d;&#x000a;\par \pard\qc OWB/Discoverer Lin\f1 e\f0 age &#x000d;&#x000a;\par \pard\ulnone If Oracle Warehouse Builder (OWB) and Discoverer Bridge have been used to \lang1033\f1 generate\lang2057\f0  your Discoverer EUL, the \f1 F\f0 older and \f1 I\f0 tem \f1 L\f0 ineage will\lang1033\f1  have been retained i\lang2057\f0 n the Discoverer EUL. &#x000d;&#x000a;\par \lang1033\f1 Using this information you can now \lang2057\f0 Hyper\f1  \f0 drill from this Discoverer \f1 W\f0 orksheet to \lang1033\f1 the respective\lang2057\f0  \f1 F\f0 older or \f1 I\f0 tem&apos;s \f1 L\f0 ineage \lang1033\f1 held \lang2057\f0 in OWB\lang1033\f1 .&#x000d;&#x000a;\par F\lang2057\f0 irst select the &apos;Business Area Name&apos; in the \f1 P\f0 age \f1 I\f0 tem\lang1033\f1 ,\lang2057\f0  \lang1033\f1 t\lang2057\f0 hen\lang1033\f1  under the column &apos;Folder Lineage&apos;  or &apos;Item Lineage&apos;\lang2057\f0  double click on the respective browser icon\lang1033\f1 , this will then reveal the folder/ items lineage in OWB.\lang2057\f0 &#x000d;&#x000a;\par \lang1033\f1 To view the database tables and columns an item is derived from, Drill from the item &apos;Item Name&apos; to &apos;Database Column&apos;.&#x000d;&#x000a;\par \lang2057\ul\b\f0 &#x000d;&#x000a;\par \lang1033\ulnone\f1 Note: &#x000d;&#x000a;\par To enable the Hyper drill,  you will first need to run the Lineage.sql script. &#x000d;&#x000a;\par Please see the release notes or the install and configuration notes for further details.\lang2057\f0 &#x000d;&#x000a;\par }&#x000d;&#x000a;" UniqueName="{C9492437-DE74-11D5-B06D-00C04FEDB835}">
